[
    {
        "quiz_metadata": {
            "title": "Kinetic & Gravitational Potential Energy Calculation Audit",
            "info_content": "<b>Energy Reference Sheet & Equations</b><br><a href=\"media/U1HW6 - W8 - Kinetic and Gravitational Potential Energy Calculations_questions.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: #008ee2; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;\">HW Paper Version</a><b> </b><br><a href=\"media/Kinetic & Potential Energy Calculations.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: #008ee2; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;\">In Class Practice - Kinetic & Potential Energy Calculations.pdf</a><b> </b><br><b>1. Gravitational Potential Energy (GPE):</b><b>\n$$\\text{GPE} = m \\times g \\times h$$</b><br><b>m (mass):</b><b> The mass of the object measured in kilograms (kg).</b><br><b>g (acceleration due to gravity):</b><b> The gravitational field strength at Earth's surface, taken as </b><b>9.8 m/s²</b><b> (unless specifically stated as 10 m/s² for approximation).</b><br><b>h (height):</b><b> The vertical elevation of the object above the reference ground level measured in meters (m).</b><br><b>GPE:</b><b> Energy stored by an object due to its vertical position in a gravitational field, measured in Joules (J).</b><br><b>2. Kinetic Energy (KE):</b><b>\n$$\\text{KE} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times m \\times v^2 = 0.5 \\times m \\times v^2$$</b><br><b>m (mass):</b><b> The mass of the moving object measured in kilograms (kg).</b><br><b>v (velocity/speed):</b><b> How fast the object is moving measured in meters per second (m/s). </b><b>Notice that velocity is squared ($v^2$)</b><b>.</b><br><b>KE:</b><b> The energy possessed by an object due to its motion, measured in Joules (J).</b><br><b>3. Conservation of Mechanical Energy:</b><b>\nIn an idealized system with no thermal losses due to friction or air resistance, total mechanical energy is conserved: $$\\text{Total Energy} = \\text{KE} + \\text{GPE} = \\text{constant}$$</b>"
        }
    },
